    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite passes (the project's Surefire config runs the acceptance tests). \n\n## Summary\n\nThe `contactPreference` field is a derived, read-only property on the owner response. I added it in the two natural, low-impact places:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` response schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field).\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` expression to the existing `toOwnerDto` method, alongside the other derived-field mappings:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\", expression = \"java(owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank() ? \\\"EMAIL\\\" : \\\"PHONE\\\")\")\n   ```\n\nThis mirrors the existing derived-field pattern (`locality`, `membershipLevel`, etc.), touches only two files, and adds a single line to a zero-complexity abstract mapper method \u2014 no method or class grows, keeping structural impact minimal. `EMAIL` when an email is present, `PHONE` otherwise. Both acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) pass, and the build is green.",
